    "summary": "Textile:  composed of six narrow strip woven lengths of cotton hand sewn together selvedge to selvedge. Plain weave: bleached white, dyed yellow, red and black cotton warps: dyed red and black cotton wefts. The cloth consists of alternating yellow, red and white warp stripes which are crossed at either end by black weft stripes. Due to the combination of warp and weft colours shades of colour rather than solid blocks of colour are created i.e. yellow warps and red wefts create a rich yellow verging on orange. The cloth is finished by unworked warps.",
